 "confidence": "high",
 "notes": "Single 22-way edge connector, rear view; the drawing names none, so it is called P1. Letters A-Z (no G, I, O, Q) and numbers 1-22 are opposite contacts, each labelled separately. Signal rows carry the same label on letter and number contact (e.g. A and 1 both 'MIC 4 IN'): read as balanced pairs, but no +/- polarity is drawn, so ports use 'a' (letter) / 'b' (number) and polarity is null. Two shield rows (E/5 and L/10) are drawn without saying which inputs they serve, so they are left with no port. 'TO A/B MIXER BUSS' (R/14, S/15) recorded as bus; 'A/B MIX OUT' (U/17, T/16) as outputs; 'A/B EXTERNAL INPUT' (N/12, M/11) as inputs. No insert is drawn. Power only on the number side: 19 -25V, 20 25V COM, 21 +25V, 22 CHASSIS; W-Z NC. Legend: NC = NOT CONNECTED. Title block: Ward-Beck Systems Ltd., M457 4X2 PRE-MIXER CONNECTOR REAR VIEW, 457-04-003, size A, ISS. 2, DATE APR 77, DRN. and CKD. signed (signature). Scan of the bound manual page, rotated 90 degrees; the facing page (faint mirror-image show-through of a schematic) is not part of this pinout. Same content as the 'Connector layout' copy."
